[0m$ [0mgh issue comment 10 --repo promikailamin/ultron_smp --body 'Implemented in commit `944205b` (pushed to `main`).

What changed:
- `run.yml` now uses the `TWINGATE_ACCESS_TOKEN` and `TWINGATE_REFRESH_TOKEN` secrets automatically.
- `TWINGATE_ENABLED` defaults to `auto`, so the connector starts when both secrets exist and skips cleanly when they do not. `false` disables it; `true` requires both secrets.
- The connector step no longer has the old `TWINGATE_ENABLED == true` gate that prevented the new secrets from activating it.
- `TWINGATE_NETWORK` is now optional: the script falls back to the access token JWT `aud` claim (the Twingate tenant/network slug). An explicit repository variable or secret still takes precedence.
- Connector output is saved to `.agent-work/logs/twingate-connector.log`; token values are still passed only via environment and a mode-600 temp env file.
- README setup instructions and the automated test were updated.

Tests actually run and passed:
- `bash -n scripts/twingate-connector.sh`
- `bash -n .agent-work/tests/test_twingate_connector.sh`
- Workflow YAML parse
- `bash .agent-work/tests/test_twingate_connector.sh` — covers auto-start, auto-skip, explicit-required mode, network derivation from the token, token non-leakage, temp-file cleanup and stop/status handling.

Remaining limitation: a real Twingate end-to-end connection was not tested because the actual connector tokens and Admin Console Resource are not available to this run. Create/assign the Minecraft Resource in the Twingate Admin Console for the private address. Public players should continue using the existing public tunnel.' 2>&1
